  "name": "development rung, full top norm byte (T32 / d384 / f512, 12 heads of 32 over 4 KV heads)",
  "norm_top_limb_is_full_byte": true,
  "note": "LANE STAGE 31: rung-P2's shape with ONE axis moved, the head dimension from 8 to 32, and what must follow from it. The norm window is NORM_TN + 1 + bit_length(isqrt(1 + width * 32767^2)), so it crosses from 31 to 32 bits exactly when the width passes 256; at width 384 it is 32 = 8 * limbs_norm and `norm_top_is_full_byte` is TRUE, which is correction C-6: the four `scaled(top, 1 << (8 ln - wrho))` lookups have coefficient 1, are the same Lk as the `byte(top)` lookups already emitted, and are dropped. Dom::D therefore carries 34 lookups per position instead of 38 and 17 helper planes instead of 19, and the H plane list is 50 planes instead of 52. hidden = 512 is the smallest power of two above the width, which keeps Dom::F unpadded and keeps an upper hidden half for the dense fixture; tokens, log_cols, inv_rate and F_E are rung-P2's, so wrho_s stays 17 and limbs_sigma_s stays 3 and the ONLY lookup family that differs from rung-P2 anywhere is Dom::D. Dom::T (2^5), Dom::Kv (32 * 4 * 32 = 2^12) and Dom::F (32 * 512 = 2^14) are exact powers of two, so this shape ALSO carries stage 30's unpadded arm, on 125M's own padded-domain set",
